  "id": "DrugBank_DB00939 - MONDO_6816",
  "verbalization": "Meclofenamic Acid is associated with Arthropathy through a chain of indications that link it to Rheumatoid Arthritis, which in turn is linked to various drugs that ultimately contribute to arthropathic conditions. The evidence suggests that Meclofenamic Acid may be repurposed for conditions where arthropathy is a manifestation, such as in Rheumatoid Arthritis, which is a known cause of arthropathy. The presence of multiple pathways, including the use of Ketoprofen, Choline Magnesium Trisalicylate, and Tolmetin, all of which are indicated to cause arthropathy, implies a potential mechanism by which Meclofenamic Acid could influence arthropathy through its effects on inflammatory or metabolic pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Meclofenamic Acid in modulating inflammatory processes that contribute to arthropathy, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
